    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras roster enters today with **Christian Yelich** leading the charge as our premier offensive anchor. With a score of 75.84, **Christian Yelich** benefits from a high-leverage leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against McGreevy, whose 4.54 xERA provides ample opportunity for production. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** demands attention at 71.03; while he faces a tougher arm in Kremer, the 16% park factor boost and his elite speed profile\u2014which we weigh heavily for SB accumulation\u2014make him a cornerstone of today's efficiency strategy. **Dillon Dingler** (63.90) and **Josh Smith** (62.54) also project as strong starts, with **Josh Smith** specifically gaining a hidden-gem edge due to Ure\u00f1a\u2019s slow delivery, which significantly improves our probability of stealing bases in this 5x5 format.\n\nNavigating the remainder of the lineup, **Junior Caminero** remains a must-start at 61.45 despite a difficult matchup against Cole, as his ability to consistently maintain an xwOBA above .370 provides the necessary floor. The most difficult bench decision involved **Casey Schmitt**, whose 43.52 efficiency fell just short of our rotation threshold; he was ultimately pushed out by the higher-upside profiles of **Luke Raley** and **Carson Benge**, whose platoon advantages against their respective right-handed opponents provide a clearer path to counting stats. We continue to monitor the status of **Trea Turner**, who remains sidelined, ensuring our depth pieces are properly positioned to mitigate any volatility. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but we are keeping a close eye on the confirmed lineups for **Yordan Alvarez**, whose L/L platoon disadvantage against Griffin slightly tempers his raw talent projection.",
